ew, 72 pieces of jewelry and 90 looks were selected for the showcase. Taking its cue from China's 24 solar terms, the runway presentation traced the changing seasons. Designers looked to traditional ceramics and other decorative objects, reinterpreting their motifs, glaze colors and forms through contemporary cuts and tailoring. The resulting looks evoked the shifting moods and rhythms of the traditional seasonal calendar. Four themed markets accompanied the show: \"Tilling: Sustaining the Body,\" \"Reading: Grounding the Mind,\" \"Fishing and Woodcutting: Nourishing the Spirit\" and \"Heaven and Earth: Returning to Nature.\" Together, they featured traditional crafts and heritage-inspired designs, long-established brands and local cuisine. Building on the cultural vision of the 2025 cross-platform program \"Neo-Chinese Style\", the event brought fashion into a historic architectural setting, connecting traditional craftsmanship and established Chinese brands with contemporary design. Conceived as a national showcase for new work in Chinese fashion, it sought to encourage international cultural exchange and introduce contemporary Chinese style to wider audiences around the world.", "content": "ONLY AVAILABLE IN PAID PLANS", "keywords": ["ent", "art", "hou", "tex", "pub"], "creator": ["cision pr newswire"], "language": "english", "country": ["laos", "bangladesh", "qatar", "turkmenistan", "afghanistan", "armenia", "brunei", "bhutan", "united arab emirates", "syria", "romania", "macau", "vietnam", "bahrain", "taiwan", "philippines", "tajikistan", "india", "yemen", "azerbaijan", "saudi arabia", "turkey", "timor-leste", "uzbekistan", "singapore", "hong kong", "china", "pakistan"], "category": ["top", "lifestyle"], "datatype": "pressrelease", "pubDate": "2026-11-04 14:20:00", "pubDateTZ": "UTC", "fetched_at": "2026-11-04 14:26:28", "image_url": "https://mmx.prnasia.com/media/MS2027227/20261102085011EST_image_1.jpg?id=OA3057903&p=medium600", "video_url": null, "source_id":